From 36533db120d6a5524b2b1989ad2bfa9a28e92c21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bogdan Lapadat <lapadat.bogdanv@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:19:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qwen35 hybrid: unsloth UD-IQ2_XXS experts (IQ1_S gate/up,
 IQ2_XXS/IQ2_XS/IQ2_S/IQ1_S downs), split MTP staging

unsloth's Ornith-1.5-122B UD-IQ2_XXS mixes the routed experts per layer: gate/up IQ1_S (layers 0-8), IQ2_XXS,
IQ2_S, IQ3_XXS; down IQ1_S, IQ2_XXS, IQ2_XS, IQ2_S, IQ3_XXS; the MTP block Q8_0 (n_embd 3072, expert FF 1024).

GPU decode experts (iq_kernels.cu): IQ1_S as a gate/up and down format (Fmt<19>, a decode-once Split<19>, the
2048-word grid staged like IQ1_M, dq_iq1_s for the FP16 prompt path and the embedding reader, row bytes), and
IQ2_XXS / IQ2_XS / IQ2_S / IQ1_S added to the down formats (their existing dots).  The IQ1_S dot is llama.cpp's
vec_dot_iq1_s_q8_1 except for the delta term: llama.cpp multiplies it by the q8_1 block's stored fp16 sum of the
unrounded activations, and as an IQ1_S weight is d (g + delta) with delta near -1 that term nearly cancels the grid
term, so the fp16 rounding shows (a real layer-0 expert: 2.7e-2 relative error against a float expert, ggml-cpu's
dot 1.5e-2).  Here the sum is the quantized one (dp4a, as ggml's own IQ1_M dot and ggml-cpu's Q8_K block sums):
1.0e-2.  The HIP FP16 dequantizer writes the sign of a zero block scale's outputs explicitly (as dq_q2_0 does).
The existing formats' kernels are unchanged.

CPU pool: no change needed; native_fmt takes any type with a ggml-cpu vec_dot (IQ1_S and the IQ2 downs run
ggml-cpu's AVX2 dots; the IQ2/IQ3 gate/up keep the AVX2 multi-token kernels).

Prompt MMQ: IQ1_S added to the MMQ types (llama.cpp's mmq-instance-iq1_s; the IQ2 types were there).

Loader: block geometry of IQ1_S (gguf_reader), and the layout check takes trailing unit dimensions as the same
tensor (unsloth stores ffn_gate_inp_shexp as [n_embd, 1]).

Streamed prompts: the staging buffers are sized for the main layers; an MTP block larger than that (Q8_0 here,
2.5 GiB, 2.8x the largest main layer) is streamed alone as two halves, one per buffer, and its MMQ products run per
half (the entries are sorted by expert, the bounds absolute rows).  Before, the Q8_0 block doubled the pinned host
staging and the borrowed VRAM: with MTP on, the long prompt swapped (23-70 tok/s) on 32 GB.

Tests: native_expert_parity takes --dims N_EMBD N_FF (synthetic) and the model's own expert geometry (real rows),
and refuses a pair the GPU kernels do not take; native_grouped_parity, iq_multi_parity and hip_prefill_mmq_parity
cover IQ1_S and the new downs at Ornith's shapes.
